{"task":"transcribe","language":"english","duration":42.11000061035156,"text":"The last picture of the museums is not a painting, it is the staircase you leave by. The architect Giuseppe Momo designed it in 1932 as the exit, and it is two staircases wound inside each other like two snakes. People going up never meet people coming down. Its circle is about 15 meters across, with an opening in the middle and a glass roof that pours light all the way down. The idea is far older. In 1505, Bermonte made a double spiral ramp without steps in the same palace, so the Pope could ride up to his rooms in his carriage. Look down from the top before you descend. The staircase looks like a seashell.","words":[{"word":"The","start":0,"end":0.3799999952316284},{"word":"last","start":0.3799999952316284,"end":0.7799999713897705},{"word":"picture","start":0.7799999713897705,"end":1.159999966621399},{"word":"of","start":1.159999966621399,"end":1.340000033378601},{"word":"the","start":1.340000033378601,"end":1.5800000429153442},{"word":"museums","start":1.5800000429153442,"end":1.9199999570846558},{"word":"is","start":1.9199999570846558,"end":2.359999895095825},{"word":"not","start":2.359999895095825,"end":2.5799999237060547},{"word":"a","start":2.5799999237060547,"end":3.0999999046325684},{"word":"painting","start":3.0999999046325684,"end":3.0999999046325684},{"word":"it","start":3.4200000762939453,"end":3.680000066757202},{"word":"is","start":3.680000066757202,"end":3.819999933242798},{"word":"the","start":3.819999933242798,"end":4.119999885559082},{"word":"staircase","start":4.119999885559082,"end":4.519999980926514},{"word":"you","start":4.519999980926514,"end":4.800000190734863},{"word":"leave","start":4.800000190734863,"end":5.019999980926514},{"word":"by","start":5.019999980926514,"end":5.340000152587891},{"word":"The","start":5.940000057220459,"end":6.079999923706055},{"word":"architect","start":6.079999923706055,"end":6.559999942779541},{"word":"Giuseppe","start":6.559999942779